# Testing Guidelines

## Framework

[Vitest](https://vitest.dev). The template ships with `vitest` configured; run with `npm test`.

- `npm test` — full run.
- `npm test -- --watch` — watch mode for active development.
- `npm test -- --changed` — only re-run tests whose source-of-truth changed since `main`.
- `npm test -- modules/<name>` — module-scoped run.

## Test file co-location

Co-locate unit tests with the code under test:

```
modules/posts/
├── services/PostService.ts
├── services/PostService.test.ts        # service unit tests
├── routes.ts
└── routes.test.ts                      # route integration tests
```

Integration tests that span modules live under `tests/integration/`.

## Service unit tests (fake DB)

For service-level tests, mock the DB at the lowest level — you're testing service logic, not Drizzle:

```ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from "vitest";
import { PostService } from "./PostService";

describe("PostService", () => {
  it("filters out soft-deleted rows by default", async () => {
    const fakeDb = { query: { posts: { findMany: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue([]) } } };
    const service = new PostService(fakeDb as any);
    await service.list({});
    expect(fakeDb.query.posts.findMany).toHaveBeenCalledWith(
      expect.objectContaining({ where: expect.anything() })
    );
  });
});
```

For multi-method flows, use `testcontainers` against a real Postgres (see integration tests below).

## Route integration tests (full chain)

Test the full middleware chain (auth → permission → validate → handler → service) via `app.request(...)` against the chained Hono app. The framework's reference modules ship a harness — mirror that shape:

```ts
import { describe, it, expect } from "vitest";
import { app } from "../../index"; // your composed app

describe("POST /posts", () => {
  it("rejects unauthenticated requests", async () => {
    const res = await app.request("/posts", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "content-type": "application/json" },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title: "x", body: "y" }),
    });
    expect(res.status).toBe(401);
  });

  it("creates a post for an authenticated user with permission", async () => {
    const res = await app.request("/posts", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "content-type": "application/json", cookie: signedAuthCookie() },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title: "x", body: "y" }),
    });
    expect(res.status).toBe(201);
    const json = await res.json();
    expect(json).toMatchObject({ id: expect.any(String), title: "x" });
  });
});
```

`signedAuthCookie()` is a test helper you write once that mints a valid session cookie via the framework's `JwtSigner`. Keep helpers in `tests/helpers/`.

## Real-DB integration tests

For tests that exercise queries / migrations / transactions against a real Postgres, use `@testcontainers/postgresql`:

```ts
import { PostgreSqlContainer } from "@testcontainers/postgresql";

let container: StartedPostgreSqlContainer;
beforeAll(async () => { container = await new PostgreSqlContainer().start(); });
afterAll(async () => { await container.stop(); });
```

Run integration tests under a separate Vitest config (`vitest.integration.config.ts`) so they don't slow the regular suite.

## Mocking

- **Mock at boundaries, not internals.** Mock the framework's `AuthProvider`, `Cache`, `JobQueue` — not your own service methods. If you find yourself mocking your own service heavily, the test is at the wrong level.
- Use `vi.fn()` over `jest.fn()` (the migration is mechanical; vitest exposes `vi`).
- Use `vi.spyOn(obj, "method").mockReturnValue(...)` for method spies — don't reassign methods directly.

## What to assert

- **Status codes + response shape**, not exact response bodies. Use `toMatchObject` over `toEqual` so non-deterministic fields (timestamps, IDs) don't make tests brittle.
- **Side effects**: did the service call the cache? Did it emit an outbox event? Did it log? Spy on those.
- **Error paths**: assert the exact AppError subclass thrown (`ConflictError`, `NotFoundError`), not just "an error was thrown".

## What NOT to do

- **Don't mock pg/Drizzle directly** in unit tests. Either go fake-DB (a hand-rolled stub object) or testcontainers. Mocking Drizzle leads to tests that pass but don't reflect SQL behavior.
- **Don't share mutable state across tests.** Each test gets a fresh fixture. If setup is expensive, use `beforeAll` + a reset in `beforeEach`.
- **Don't test framework internals** — those are tested in `@sixthsummit/ship-api`'s own test suite. You test your code.
- **Don't add tests just for coverage.** A test that asserts trivia (`expect(x).toBeDefined()`) is worse than no test — it lies about what's verified.

## Coverage

The template ships with no enforced coverage gate; opt in by editing `vitest.config.ts` if you want a floor. The framework itself targets 80% line / 70% branch on `packages/core/src/**` per `docs/V4_STATUS.md` — your app can do whatever fits the team.
